<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="153" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>A Do item closed because someone satisfied it writes a Routine Decision Record naming them (D-145b)</title>
    <phase>4 Decision Record</phase>
    <gate>blocked: #1907 (task 149) merged into docs/ontology-platform-design (same writer file)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New secure-family record write from the nightly job; extends the single Decision Record create path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Adds a writer entry point under the D-34 single-create-site guard and secure-family ownership; attribution rules need judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <deps>149</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,job,dataverse,security,testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>When a Do item's underlying work is done outside the decision route (someone completes the To Do on its form, records the work-assignment response), the nightly pass closes the Signal as ConditionCleared with no Decision Record and with `sprk_resolvedby`/`sprk_confirmedby` null (`SignalWriter.cs:854` "a system closure has no Decision Record"; `SignalClosureService.cs:41-43`; called from `SignalReevaluationJob.cs:387`). The owner decided (D-145b): that closure is recorded, naming the person who did the work.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF engineer.</role>
  <goal>Every Do-lane Signal the nightly pass closes as ConditionCleared gets exactly one Routine Decision Record that names, best effort, the user who changed the underlying record; nothing else about system closures changes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-145, D-129, D-34, D-123, D-139 (notes/decisions.md). Task 149's `WriteGateDecisionAsync` is the nearest precedent: a non-commit entry point on `DecisionRecordWriter`, an idempotency key in `sprk_steps`, ownership through `RecordOwnershipResolver`, one CreateAsync site pinned by `DecisionRecordContextImmutabilityTests`. Re-read the merged 149 code at your base.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalClosureService.cs and SignalWriter.cs (ConditionCleared close)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReevaluationJob.cs (:387 caller)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionRecordWriter.cs (REFERENCE: WriteGateDecisionAsync from 149 — copy its shape)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>DecisionRecordWriter (commit and gate entry points); SignalClosureService closes ConditionCleared Signals.</existing>
    <extension>Add one writer entry point and call it from the existing closure; no new service, route, registration or column.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Do item closed by a colleague leaves no record of who closed it or why, contrary to D-145b.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-145b">Scope: Do-lane Signals closed as ConditionCleared only. Superseded, PolicyRetired and Decide/Know-lane closures stay record-free, unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-145b">Record class Routine; `sprk_action` null; the Signal links to the record (`sprk_decisionrecord`) and `sprk_resolvedby` is set when the person is known. Attribution, best effort, from the subject row the predicate read: the user in its `modifiedby` as read by the closing pass. If that user is an application user or the Spaarke service identity, or the read fails, write the record with `sprk_confirmedby` null and a reason saying the person is unknown; never guess, never use the assignee or the owner (D-129).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-139 / 149">Exactly one record per Signal closure: deterministic idempotency key from the Signal id and its episode, stored the way 149 stores its key; a re-run of the nightly pass writes nothing new. The key must not collide with 149's gate key (different prefix) and 149's gate lookup must still match only gate records (it filters `sprk_confirmedby` Null plus its key; check both still hold).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-34">One CreateAsync site in DecisionRecordWriter; the immutability ArchTests stay green, extended for the new entry point if needed, never weakened.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-123 / D-33">Ownership via RecordOwnershipResolver exactly as the other entry points do; a Signal in a secure family produces a secure-child record. Logs carry counts and type names only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-61">No extra writes to unchanged Signals; the record write happens only on a real close.</constraint>
    <constraint source="fail-closed">A failure to write the record does not block or undo the close; it is logged and counted on `ontology.writer.failures` (the 035 alert sees it) and retried on the next pass through the idempotent key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Publish-size delta vs a fresh build of origin/master, no new HIGH CVE; report the added Dataverse requests per closed Signal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-123">uac-r2 reviews the PR (SendMessage + #1355).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Re-read the ConditionCleared close path and 149's gate entry point at your base.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the writer entry point and the attribution read; call it from the closure.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests (filtered), seeding proof on idempotency, size delta, PR into docs/ontology-platform-design.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A colleague completes Alice's To Do on its form; the nightly pass closes Alice's Do Signal and writes one Routine record with `sprk_confirmedby` = the colleague, linked to the Signal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Running the pass again writes nothing new.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`modifiedby` is an application user or the read fails: one record with `sprk_confirmedby` null and the unknown-person reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: Superseded, PolicyRetired and a Decide-lane ConditionCleared write no record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A secure-family Do Signal's record is a secure child (owned as the other entry points own it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record-write failure leaves the Signal closed and is counted on `ontology.writer.failures`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">149's gate idempotency tests and the single-create-site ArchTests stay green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Test scope: the cases above only; seeding proof on the idempotency key.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If attribution needs audit-history reads or a new column, STOP and report the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the change requires editing uac-r2's files, STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
</task>
